-- title:
--   Base change of the function field along an F-algebra map
-- statement:
--   Let $F$, $K$, $K'$ be fields with $K$ and $K'$ given $F$-algebra structures, let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $F$, and let $f \colon K \to K'$ be an $F$-algebra homomorphism. Write $W\!\restriction\!K$ and $W\!\restriction\!K'$ (in Lean, `W⁄K` and `W⁄K'`) for the affine Weierstrass curves obtained from $W$ by base change to $K$ and to $K'$, with coordinate rings the quotients of the bivariate polynomial rings $K[X][Y]$, resp. $K'[X][Y]$, by the ideal generated by the Weierstrass polynomial, and function fields the fraction fields of these coordinate rings. The assertion is that there exists a ring homomorphism $\Phi$ from the function field of $W\!\restriction\!K$ to the function field of $W\!\restriction\!K'$ with the following property: for every $p \in K[X][Y]$, the value of $\Phi$ on the image in the function field of the class of $p$ in the coordinate ring equals the image in the function field of $W\!\restriction\!K'$ of the class of the polynomial obtained from $p$ by applying $f$ to all coefficients (the map induced on $K[X][Y]$ by the coefficientwise map $K[X] \to K'[X]$). No further property of $\Phi$, such as $F$-linearity, injectivity or uniqueness, is asserted.
--
--   This is the functoriality of the affine coordinate ring and function field of a Weierstrass curve under extension of the base field, in the form needed to compare rational functions on $W$ over two extensions of $F$. It is used in the proof that the Weil pairing on a Weierstrass curve is unchanged under an embedding of base fields ([`WeierstrassCurve.Affine.weilPairing0_map_algHom`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.Affine.weilPairing0_map_algHom)).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_Affine_exists_ringHom_functionField_baseChange_of_algHom.lean

import Mathlib
